{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation landed through Gerrit change 2952.\n\nEvidence:\n- Plan review passed and ticket was claimed before code work.\n- Commit `35e6e5714c0b2b3ad03cc8464d2d969c97c1f068` merged to `origin/main` with `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, and `0` unresolved comments.\n- Local validation before push: targeted MCP/doctor/config tests passed (`32 passed, 3 skipped` after the final review fix); `make lint` passed; `make typecheck` passed; `rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD` passed. Full `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` was attempted earlier and completed only to unrelated local/baseline/environment failures documented in the session log, while Gerrit Verified passed on the submitted patchset.\n- Project config verification from merged worktree `/Users/joeoakhart/mcp-project-bubblefish`: `codex mcp get rebar` resolves repo config using `MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX`; `copilot mcp list` shows `rebar` under workspace/repository-scoped servers, not user servers.\n- Machine-local cutover completed after merge: removed `rebar` from `~/.copilot/mcp-config.json` (kept `atlassian`, `serena`); removed global `mcpServers.rebar` from `~/.claude.json` without touching `projects.*`; removed `[mcp_servers.rebar]` from `~/.codex/config.toml`.\n- Non-project verification from `/Users/joeoakhart`: `codex mcp get rebar` reports no server named `rebar`; `copilot mcp list` shows only user `serena` and `atlassian`; global Claude config has no `mcpServers.rebar`.\n- Requested `~/rebar` verification note: `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar` is intentionally read-only for this session and is currently behind `origin/main`, so it does not yet contain the merged `.mcp.json`; I did not modify it. The merged project worktree verification above exercises the landed repo config.\n\nDocs touched: `docs/mcp-client-setup.md`, `docs/mcp-auth.md`, `infra/runbooks/mcp-client-pats.md`, `examples/mcp-clients/README.md`, example client config files, and `mcp-clients.local.example.json`."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789017238111018001,"uuid":"d3a3d2c7-ae31-4a09-be07-42b472cc6d39"}